        "detail": "A perianal abscess is at the anal verge, below Hilton's line, and can be felt between an index finger in the canal and a thumb over the swelling externally — it is generally less painful, since the overlying skin here expands more easily. An ischiorectal abscess produces excruciating throbbing pain beside the anal canal with a brawny, oedematous swelling, tender with or without obvious fluctuation; do not wait for fluctuation to appear before acting.",
