        "stage": "The three mechanisms",
        "title": "Embolism, thrombosis, and non-occlusive low flow",
        "detail": "They differ in speed of onset and in the patient they affect. Non-occlusive ischaemia occurs in the shocked or critically ill patient without any blockage at all.",
