        "detail": "Scarring from chronic duodenal ulceration is classical, but in Indian series corrosive injury and gastroduodenal tuberculosis account for a large share of cases, and outcomes with tuberculosis are actually good once recognised and treated. Malignancy, chronic pancreatitis, and a pancreatic mass are also causes, especially in older patients.",
