        "id": "h7",
        "stage": "Decision",
        "title": "Medical management of reflux for the sliding type; surgical repair considered for the rolling type or complications",
        "detail": "A sliding hernia found incidentally without symptoms is usually left alone. A paraoesophageal hernia is more often discussed for repair given its risk of strangulation, even before symptoms force the issue.",
