        "detail": "Unlike hereditary spherocytosis, the red cells here start out structurally normal. The patient's own antibodies attach to them and mark them for destruction — this is an acquired, not inherited, process, and it is worth asking about directly since the two conditions are otherwise easy to confuse on a first pass.",
