        "stage": "Examination",
        "title": "The spleen is palpable in only about half of patients",
        "detail": "This is a genuinely useful negative — a normal-sized spleen does not argue against this diagnosis the way it might for some other haemolytic anaemias. The liver may also be palpable, and generalised lymph node enlargement is sometimes present.",
