        "id": "a8",
        "stage": "Decision",
        "title": "Urgent referral to a specialist team; chemoradiotherapy is the primary treatment for most anal canal cancer",
        "detail": "This differs from rectal cancer, where surgery leads — anal canal squamous carcinoma is treated primarily with combined chemotherapy and radiotherapy, with surgery reserved for selected situations. The distinction is worth knowing because the two cancers, sitting centimetres apart, are managed quite differently.",
