        "stage": "Recognise the venous complications",
        "title": "Renal vein invasion can cause a new varicocele or leg swelling",
        "detail": "Occlusion of the left renal or testicular vein can produce a varicocele of recent onset, and inferior vena cava occlusion can cause bilateral leg oedema — both worth actively asking about, since they point directly at venous spread.",
