        "stage": "Examination",
        "title": "An enlarged kidney may be palpable; tenderness is notably absent",
        "detail": "A small tumour at the upper pole can push the whole kidney down, making the lower pole easier to feel than expected. If cystoscopy is performed during an episode of bleeding, it can identify which kidney the blood is coming from.",
