        "id": "s4",
        "stage": "A substantial number of stones are genuinely silent",
        "title": "Particularly phosphate stones, which can grow to fill the collecting system as a staghorn calculus",
        "detail": "These patients may present with unrelated gastrointestinal symptoms, with established infection or uraemia by the time of diagnosis, or purely incidentally on an X-ray taken for something else entirely.",
