        "title": "A silent, small, non-obstructing stone may simply be monitored; a staghorn calculus, an obstructing stone, or one with superimposed infection needs active treatment",
        "detail": "Untreated staghorn disease carries a real risk of progressive kidney damage and infection, which is why silence is not the same as safety for this particular stone type. Specific intervention is a urological decision based on stone burden, position and renal function.",
