        "stage": "Distinguish from other prostatic conditions",
        "title": "The symptom overlap with benign prostatic hyperplasia and prostate cancer is real",
        "detail": "A gland that is hard, irregular, or has an obliterated median sulcus points away from simple prostatitis and towards a diagnosis that needs to be actively excluded rather than assumed away.",
