        "id": "t3",
        "stage": "Ask about exciting causes, though their absence proves nothing",
        "title": "Straining at stool, lifting a heavy weight, coitus, or a blow to the scrotum during activity such as cycling",
        "detail": "These act through violent contraction of the spirally attached cremaster muscle, which favours rotation of the testis around its vertical axis. Many cases have no identifiable trigger at all.",
