        "stage": "Confirm with fluctuation and translucency",
        "title": "The hallmark tests for a fluid-filled swelling",
        "detail": "The translucency test must be performed correctly — the torch or light source is held behind the swelling, not in front of it, or the testis obstructing the light path will produce a false negative. An uncomplicated hydrocele and an epididymal cyst both transilluminate well; a spermatocele does not, because its contained fluid is not clear.",
