        "stage": "If the testis can be felt separately from the swelling, reconsider the diagnosis",
        "title": "This points towards an epididymal cyst or spermatocele rather than a true hydrocele",
        "detail": "A true hydrocele surrounds the body of the testis, making it impalpable within the fluid; feeling the testis distinctly and separately changes the diagnosis.",
