        "stage": "Know the recognised complications",
        "title": "Rupture (traumatic or spontaneous), haematocele from injury, infection leading to a suppurated hydrocele, and, rarely, herniation of the hydrocele sac itself",
        "detail": "Each of these changes the clinical picture and the management, so a hydrocele that has changed in character — become tender, discoloured, or acutely painful — is reassessed rather than assumed to be behaving as before.",
